course: dictionary
lesson: 8003
title: Redshift
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Light travels in waves, and our eyes see those waves as colours. Red is at one end of the rainbow and blue is at the other. Redshift is the word for what happens to light when a star or galaxy is moving away from us.
explain: «Light from a galaxy moving away from us is stretched to redder colours, called redshift.» Stretched means the light waves are pulled longer, so the light moves towards the red end of the rainbow. The galaxy is not really turning red; the light reaching Earth just looks redder.
explain: The amount of redshift tells us how fast the galaxy is moving: «the amount tells how fast it is moving.» Scientists use redshift to study the universe, and it is evidence that the universe is expanding.
fact: Redshift is when light from a star or galaxy moving away from us is stretched so it looks redder.
fact: Redshift shifts light towards the red end of the rainbow.
fact: Redshift is evidence that the universe is expanding.
fact: Redshift supports the Big Bang theory, the idea that the universe began long ago and has been growing ever since.
fact: The more redshift a galaxy shows, the faster it is moving away from us.
exercise: What is redshift? | *Light from a moving galaxy being stretched so it looks redder | A star that is hotter than the Sun | A colour you can see only at night | Light that gets stronger as it gets closer
exercise: Light from a galaxy moving away from us looks redder. What is this called? | Starlight | Blueshift | *Redshift | Sunrise
exercise: Redshift is evidence for something big about space. What is it? | Stars are all the same colour | The Moon is getting smaller | *The universe is expanding | Rainbows are made in space
test: What does the amount of redshift tell us? | The colour of the galaxy | *How fast the galaxy is moving | How many stars are in it | How far away the Sun is
test: Which theory does redshift support? | The water cycle | Germ theory | Photosynthesis | *The Big Bang theory
exam: «Light from a galaxy moving away from us is stretched to redder colours, called redshift.» Which word means light stretched so it looks redder? | Eclipse | Shadow | Dimming | *Redshift
